# A load that fails answers open_file with the loader's reason, not just the path, lists no dataset and keeps no
# label: the same file name loaded next is the plain name, not "(2)". The fixture MCAP has a channel and no message,
# which the MCAP plugin refuses itself; a plugin that succeeds with no data fails the same way (FileLoaderTest
# "YieldsNoData" cases), since a desktop CI plugin with that shape does not exist.
# needs: plugins
refuse open_file {"path":"$CHECKOUT/scripts/qa/regressions/fixtures/no_messages/ros2_occupancy_real.mcap"}
expect No channels could be bound
get_status {}
absent ros2_occupancy_real
open_file {"path":"$CHECKOUT/tests/wasm/fixtures/ros2_occupancy_real.mcap"}
expect "loaded":true
until get_status {} "name":"ros2_occupancy_real.mcap"
absent ros2_occupancy_real.mcap (2)
